w('ART_DIRECTION_BIBLE.md', '''## Identity
Dark crusader fantasy meets undead apocalypse. Grounded 13th-century kit (mail, surcoats, great helms, heater shields) as the readable "hero" language; the world around it is ruined, fog-choked and lit by fire and a dying sun.

## Proportions & silhouette
Humanoids 1.80-1.90 m, slightly heroic shoulders. Silhouettes must read side-on at gameplay distance: helm shape, cape and weapon carry the read. Enemies get distinct postures (hunched walkers, low crawlers, top-heavy brutes) rather than recolours.

## Materials (Unreal: M_SB_Surface master + MI_* instances)
One master material with procedural grime (noise-driven, pre-skinned position on characters so it does not swim), micro-roughness variation, optional procedural chainmail ring pattern and emissive. Palette: Steel, SteelDark, Chainmail, Leather, ClothWhite, ClothRed, Gold, Visor, Wood, WoodDead, Stone, StoneDark, Iron, Ember, Bone, Flesh, Gore, Rags. Rule: never more than one hero-saturated colour (crusader red) per character; everything else desaturated.

## Lighting
Low warm key (dusk sun ~7 deg), cool moon rim from behind, warm practical fire light near the play lane, volumetric height fog for depth layering. Play lane always brighter than background.

## Camera
Side-on 2.5D, perspective CineCamera ~30 mm at ~7.6 m, play axis = world X, background layers at -Y, foreground framing only at screen edges.

## Composition layers
Foreground framing (rocks) -> play lane -> midground storytelling (graves, banners, braziers, litter) -> curtain wall/gate/towers -> far tower silhouettes.
''')
w('BLENDER_PIPELINE.md', '''## Situation
Blender 5.2.3 LTS is connected through the Blender MCP add-on (verified 2026-11-04).

## Blender stage (working, verified)
`unreal/Scripts/blender/sb_blender_lookdev.py` imports the sbkit glTF exports into Blender, replaces the flat glTF materials with full procedural node materials (AO-driven cavity grime and edge polish, tarnish, anisotropic scratch roughness, hammered micro-bump on steel; real ring bump on chainmail; weave bump, stain and hem mud on cloth; grain on leather/wood; voronoi block detail on stone), bone-parents the sword (hand_r) and shield (lowerarm_l), builds a look-dev stage (sky, warm key, cool rim, fill) and saves `SourceArt/Blender/HeroKnight_Lookdev.blend` next to the Unreal project. Renders go to `SourceArt/Blender/renders/`.

## Current pipeline (working, verified)
`unreal/Scripts/lib/sbkit.py` is a dependency-free Python modelling + rigging kit (lathe, bevelled slab, sphere, extrude, quad-grid surfaces, smooth normals, arc-length UVs, 4-bone skin weights, skeleton, baked keyframe animation) that writes glTF 2.0. The same modules run inside Unreal's Python, so assets are generated on the user's machine and imported by `sb_ue_import.py` (Interchange glTF -> SkeletalMesh/Skeleton/PhysicsAsset/AnimSequence or StaticMesh).

## When Blender is available
Open Blender with the MCP add-on server running. The same glTF files import into Blender (File > Import > glTF) for sculpting, retopology, UV refinement and texture baking; source .blend files are then kept under `art/blender/` and exported back to glTF/FBX with: scale 1.0 (metres), +Y up, apply transforms, armature root `root`, UE bone naming.
''')
w('UNREAL_ARCHITECTURE.md', '''## Engine
%s. Rendering: Lumen GI/reflections, Virtual Shadow Maps, Nanite for static environment meshes, volumetric fog, SkyAtmosphere + VolumetricCloud.

## Content layout
/Game/SteelAndBlood/{Characters/Player, Weapons, Environments/RuinedCastle, Materials/Master, Materials/Instances, Levels, Tools}

## Automation
- `BP_PyRunner` (EditorUtilityActor): construction script executes `Saved/SB/boot.py`, which runs one queued `run.py`. Long editor operations (spawning, level changes) are deferred to the next Slate tick.
- `unreal/Scripts/lib/*.py` are fetched from this repo by commit SHA, so every Unreal change is reproducible from git.

## Gameplay plan (Blueprint-first; C++ when a compiler path exists)
GameMode `BP_SBGameMode`, `BP_SBPlayerController` (Enhanced Input), `BP_HeroKnight` (Character, plane-constrained to X/Z), components: `BPC_Health`, `BPC_Combat` (montage-driven hit windows via AnimNotifyStates), `BPC_Equipment` (data-driven from DataTables converted from src/data/items.js), `BPC_Stamina`. Enemies: shared `BP_ZombieBase` + per-type DataAssets, StateTree/Behavior Tree AI. SaveGame: `SG_SteelAndBlood` mirroring the browser save schema.
''' % UE)
